# Extra tests: commutativity + array references
#
# Commutativity: x = a * b and y = b * a are the same value.
# Arrays: two identical loads A[t1] are a CSE; a store to A kills the cache.

# --- commutativity ---
x = a * b
y = b * a          # same as x  (commutative)
p = m + n
q = n + m          # same as p  (commutative)

# --- array references (from the PDF CFG example) ---
i = 0
t1 = 4 * i
t3 = A[t1]
t5 = A[t1]         # same as t3  (redundant load, CSE)
t6 = t3 * t5

# store kills cached load, so the next load is NOT redundant
A[t1] = t6
t7 = A[t1]         # must be recomputed (not deleted)
